  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPVO &#x2013; REACH &#x2013; Rural Empowerment and Comprehensive Healthcare for coffee farmers in the Greater Masaka Region, Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JDE Peet&apos;s (JDE), Sucafina, a global coffee merchant, and UGACOF a leading coffee processor in Uganda, have partnered with Elucid, an organisation specialising in implementing scalable healthcare solutions in supply chains, to address critical risks in the coffee sector through the REACH project.Focused on healthcare, this initiative aims to improve the health and livelihoods of over 3,000 coffee farming families in Uganda&apos;s Greater Masaka Region.Uganda&apos;s coffee sector depends heavily on smallholders, many of whom face low incomes, limited healthcare access, and financial instability. Over 40% live below the international poverty line and 98% lack health insurance, leaving families vulnerable to high out-of-pocket healthcare costs. These financial pressures push 25% of farming households deeper into poverty each year, increasing child labour risks and undermining productivity.REACH addresses these challenges through Elucid&apos;s innovative health financing platform, which subsidises essential and emergency healthcare costs and provides farmers with digital wallets for healthcare savings. Sustainability premiums delivered through the platform support financial resilience and better household management.The programme intends to create impact at both individual and structural levels. Reducing healthcare costs enables farmers to invest in farming, education, and well-being while lowering reliance on child labour. Healthcare providers benefit from stable revenue streams, enabling investments in equipment, skilled staff and expanded services. Collaboration with local and national authorities ensures these improvements are sustainable and community-wide.By addressing poor health, financial instability, and child labour, REACH strengthens farmer productivity, loyalty, and resilience, ensuring a more sustainable supply chain. This initiative not only aligns with the corporate values of JDE, Sucafina and UGACOF, but also prepares them for emerging supply chain due diligence legislation. REACH serves as a scalable blueprint for expanding healthcare solutions to more farmers in Uganda, tackling social risks, and advancing sustainability across global coffee supply chains.</narrative>
  </description>
